 the Playboy Club  was cancelled after only three episodes  The Rum Diary is another example of  heard taking a pretty typical hot girl  part and making it her own  2011 film by Bruce Robinson was based on  a hunter s Thompson book and stars  Johnny Depp as a down-on-his-luck writer  who takes a job in San Juan Puerto Rico  during the early 1960s Hurd plays a girl  he meets while he's in a boat and she's  skinny-dipping and she goes off to  become the center of a love triangle  between him as shady realtor played by  Aaron Eckhart The Rum Diary is how heard  and depth first met leading to a  relationship that started in 2012 became  a marriage in 2015 and ended in 2016  with heard filing for divorce and  accusing death of domestic abuse all the  boys love Mandy Lane is a slasher style  horror movie about an unusual high  school girl and the secrets she does her  best to keep as the other teens around  her start dying heard played the title  role and it might have been her breakout  part if the movie had come out as  originally planned it was filmed in 2006  before almost everything else on this  list where the 20 year old heard  perfectly cast as the mysterious Mandy  unfortunately the weinstein company  declined to distribute it and the  company they handed it off to went out  of business the movie went unreleased in  the United States for seven years before  finally coming out on video in 2013  after Amber Heard was enough of a star  to get people to watch it the sequel to  2010's machete was not a success at the  box office or among critics but it was  the kind of sequel that made sense for  the over-the-top character played by  Danny Trejo and the unique sensibility  of director Robert Rodriguez the  supporting cast of machete kills  features a parade of beautiful women  Amber Heard is still a standout however  she plays Blanca Vasquez a beauty queen  who's also a secret agent and machetes  handler on his mission to stop a madman  from launching a nuclear missile at  Washington DC interestingly Amber Heard  plays a glamorous government assassin  again in 2014's three days to kill but  in a slightly less outrageous context  the film stars Kevin Costner is a  veteran CIA agent with an estranged  family and terminal cancer heards  younger and more ruthless agent is  tasked with manipulating him into  hunting down one last target by offering  him an experimental cure for his illness  three days to kill is one of those aging  baby boomer action movies where an older  man proves that he still has what it  takes to get the job done  thankfully unlike some movies of this  type the protagonists focus remains on  his family  meaning that herd is never asked to be a  may-december love interest for Costner  2015's Magic Mike XXL was a phenomenon  far more so than the original magic bike  the first movie was a drama about male  strippers  whereas the sequel was a feel-good  celebration of male strippers which  unsurprisingly made it a huge hit among  women as well as gay men and pretty much  anyone who's comfortable watching  muscular men dance with their shirts off  Amber Heard was one of the many fresh  cast members to join for the sequel  playing a new love interest for Magic  Mike played by Channing Tatum at first  her photographer character seems likely  to be a one-night stand but after she  and Mike mutually decided not to have  sex she shows back up later in the movie  and they build more of a relationship  one thing that's clear and looking back  at amber heards career so far is that  she's obviously been chosen for many  roles because of how beautiful she is  however as we've seen again and again  what makes her interesting in those  roles as the intelligence she always  displays adding depth to characters who  weren't necessarily created to havening  check out one of our newest videos right  here Plus even more looper videos about  the DC extended universe are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell s